      "text_copy_1802692388": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
        "text": "<h3><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Buys time to find and treat reversible causes</span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Implementing a progressive program approach to take appropriate patients from the field to the hospital for advanced life-saving interventions, such as ECMO and PCI, resulted in an increase in survival rate with good neurological function from 8.2% to 50%.<sup>34</sup></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">LUCAS allows the healthcare provider to perform simultaneous diagnosis and treatment of reversible causes, e.g. coronary occlusion, pulmonary emboli, intoxication or accidental hypothermia.<sup>6,17,35,40</sup></span></p>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 25 2025 14:43:51 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
        "textIsRich": "true"
      }
    },
    "text_copy_1802692388": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
      "jcr:title": "Buys",
      "cq:masterBuildingBlock": true,
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Tue Jan 14 2025 22:32:19 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Jan 20 2025 16:10:32 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "cq/experience-fragments/editor/components/buildingblock",
      "text_copy_310227185": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "jcr:createdBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
        "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
        "hideComponent": "false",
        "jcr:created": "Tue Jan 14 2025 22:33:30 GMT+0000",
        "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
        "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Saves lives in the cath lab</span></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Using LUCAS during PCI, 25% vs. historical 10% of sudden cardiac arrest patients who did not respond to normal advanced resuscitation efforts, could be saved with good neurological outcome.&nbsp;This despite prolonged CPR durations of up to 50 minutes.<sup>30</sup><br>\n <br>\n </span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Life-saving PCI during LUCAS chest compressions leads to significant improvements in ROSC in cardiac arrest patients with persistent VF or non-shockable rhythms.<sup>27</sup></span></li>\n</ul>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Mar 21 2025 21:17:40 GMT+0000",
